@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Stack-safe Weisfeiler--Lehman refinement with reusable dense buffers

rectangle "Validated GraphProjection list\nforward + reverse CSR" as INPUT #F1F3F5
rectangle "Seed labels matrix A\n<latex>\ell_0(v)=mix(mix(A,d^-(v)),d^+(v))</latex>" as SEED #DBE4FF
rectangle "Allocate matrix B capacities once\nallocate canonical vocabulary once" as ALLOC #FFE8CC
rectangle "Clear each B row\nretain its allocation" as CLEAR #FFF3BF
rectangle "Iterate vertices in dense order\nsort one reusable incident-label buffer" as REFINE #D3F9D8
rectangle "Push fixed-mixer raw labels into B" as MIX #C3FAE8
rectangle "Clear + refill vocabulary\nsort, deduplicate, binary-search ranks" as CANON #E5DBFF
rectangle "Swap matrices A and B\nno graph state or native recursion" as SWAP #FFD8A8
rectangle "Return matrix A\npublic bits equal committed predecessor" as RESULT #B2F2BB
rectangle "Return seed matrix A\nzero rounds allocate no scratch buffers" as ZERO #C3FAE8

INPUT --> SEED
SEED --> ZERO : requested rounds = 0
SEED --> ALLOC : one or more rounds
ALLOC --> CLEAR
CLEAR --> REFINE
REFINE --> MIX
MIX --> CANON
CANON --> SWAP
SWAP --> CLEAR : another bounded round
SWAP --> RESULT : complete

note right of ALLOC
  Scratch ownership is call-local.
  Capacity is proportional to supplied vertices;
  nothing survives the public call.
end note

note bottom of SWAP
  Heap-resident vectors are the explicit state machine.
  Graph depth and width do not increase native call depth.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#F1F3F5>| immutable validated input |
  |<#DBE4FF>| compatibility-stable seed |
  |<#FFE8CC>| bounded call-local allocation |
  |<#FFF3BF>| allocation-retaining reset |
  |<#D3F9D8>| iterative neighborhood work |
  |<#C3FAE8>| fixed mixing or zero-round result |
  |<#E5DBFF>| deterministic canonicalization |
  |<#FFD8A8>| explicit buffer-state transition |
  |<#B2F2BB>| unchanged public result |
endlegend
@enduml
